  "build_relevance": "legacy-sop-spring-simulation",
  "last_verified": "2026-06-18",
  "key_concepts": [
    "Spring SOP is a stateful simulation over point masses and polygon edge springs.",
    "timeinc controls simulation step size and should not exceed one frame of project time.",
    "Fixed point groups can be copied from the source each frame to anchor parts of the simulation.",
    "Hooke's Law spring behavior is generally more stable than normalized displacement.",
    "Limit planes and collision inputs use hit behavior plus tangent/normal gain controls."
  ]
